1121 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 257 0 R
/E (Data is fragmented across actors and systems with limited standardization. Satellite data involves trade-offs: open data is accessible but may lack the resolution required for plot-level deforestation monitoring; commercial imagery is costly and requires significant processing capacity. Verification of field-level data remains complex and expensive to validate independently, creating vulnerability to manipulation in non-audited systems. Credibility depends less on data volume than on reliability, consistency, and governance.)
/Pg 46 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
